# Tailwind CSS & Styling Conventions

## Design System Colors

### Brand Colors (from [tailwind.config.ts](mdc:tailwind.config.ts))
```css
/* Primary Brand */
primary: hsl(355 76% 36%) /* #a21622 - Deep red */
primary-foreground: hsl(348 45% 98%) /* #fcf7f8 - Light text */

/* Secondary Brand */
secondary: hsl(210 100% 50%) /* #0085FF - Bright blue */
secondary-foreground: hsl(348 45% 98%) /* #fcf7f8 - Light text */

/* Background System */
background: hsl(0 0% 3.9%) /* #0A0A0A - Very dark */
foreground: hsl(348 45% 98%) /* #fcf7f8 - Light text */
card: hsl(0 0% 12.2%) /* #1F1F1F - Dark card background */
border: hsl(0 0% 16.5%) /* #2A2A2A - Border color */

/* Accent Colors */
amber-400: /* Used for CTA buttons and highlights */
```

## Component Styling Patterns

### className Utility Usage
Always use the `cn()` utility from [src/lib/utils.ts](mdc:src/lib/utils.ts) for conditional classes:

```typescript
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

// Good
className={cn(
  "base-classes",
  "responsive-classes sm:text-lg md:text-xl",
  conditionalClass && "conditional-styles",
  className // Allow prop overrides
)}

// Avoid
className={`base-classes ${condition ? "active" : ""} ${className}`}
```

### Responsive Design Patterns
```typescript
// Mobile-first approach with breakpoint prefixes
className="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl"

// Flex layouts with responsive direction
className="flex flex-col sm:flex-row"

// Spacing with responsive values
className="px-6 sm:px-8 md:px-12"

// Grid with responsive columns
className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"
```

### Animation Classes
Use Tailwind's built-in animations and custom ones from config:

```typescript
// Standard animations
className="transition-all duration-300 hover:scale-105"
className="animate-pulse animate-bounce"

// Custom aurora animation (defined in tailwind.config.ts)
className="animate-aurora"

// Transform utilities for interactions
className="transform hover:translate-x-1"
```

## Layout and Spacing

### Container Patterns
```typescript
// Full-width sections
className="w-full min-h-screen"

// Centered content containers
className="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"

// Full viewport sections
className="relative flex items-center justify-center w-full min-h-screen"
```

### Positioning and Z-Index
```typescript
// Video backgrounds
className="absolute inset-0 z-0 w-full h-full object-cover"

// Overlays
className="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/80 via-black/60 to-transparent z-0"

// Content over backgrounds
className="relative z-10"
```

## Button Styling Patterns

### Primary CTA Button
```typescript
className="flex items-center justify-center w-full px-8 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-black transition-transform duration-300 transform bg-amber-400 rounded-md shadow-lg sm:w-auto hover:bg-amber-300 hover:scale-105"
```

### Secondary Button
```typescript
className="flex items-center justify-center w-full px-8 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white transition-all duration-300 transform bg-transparent border-2 border-white rounded-md sm:w-auto hover:bg-white hover:text-black group"
```

### Magic Button Pattern (Gradient Border)
Use the pattern from [src/components/ui/MagicButton.tsx](mdc:src/components/ui/MagicButton.tsx):
```typescript
// Outer gradient container
className="relative inline-flex h-12 overflow-hidden rounded-full p-[1px] bg-gradient-to-r from-primary via-secondary to-primary bg-[size:400%_100%]"

// Inner content
className="flex h-full w-full items-center justify-center rounded-full px-6 font-medium bg-card text-foreground transition-all duration-300 hover:bg-opacity-80"
```

## Typography Scale
```typescript
// Headings
className="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl"
className="text-lg tracking-wide md:text-xl"

// Font weights
className="font-light font-normal font-medium font-semibold font-bold"

// Text colors with semantic meaning
className="text-foreground text-gray-200 text-amber-400"
```

## Dark Mode Support
The design system is built for dark mode by default:
- Use semantic color tokens (foreground, background, etc.)
- Avoid hardcoded colors like `text-white` except for specific design needs
- Test components in both light and dark modes